```python
def _find_distribution_name(module_name: str) -> str:
    """Translate a top-level module name into the name of the
    distribution that provides it.

    A distribution name does not always match the module it installs
    (for example the ``pytest-cov`` distribution provides the
    ``pytest_cov`` module). :func:`importlib.metadata.version` expects a
    distribution name, so look the module up in
    :func:`importlib.metadata.packages_distributions` and use the first
    distribution found. This falls back to the module name when nothing
    matches so the existing error messages keep working.
    """
    import importlib.metadata

    packages = importlib.metadata.packages_distributions()
    distributions = packages.get(module_name)

    if distributions:
        return distributions[0]

    return module_name
```

